class.description:
[XMLWriter] is the counterpart of [XMLParser]: it builds an XML document in memory, one element, attribute, text, CDATA section or comment at a time. Names are checked and text and attribute values are escaped ([code]&[/code], [code]<[/code], [code]>[/code], quotes), so the output is always well-formed. Child elements are indented with [member indent]; an element that contains text keeps its content on one line. An element without content is written as [code]<name/>[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var writer = XMLWriter.new()
writer.write_declaration()
writer.begin_element("inventory")
writer.add_attribute("owner", "Ann & Bob")
writer.begin_element("item")
writer.add_attribute("id", "sword")
writer.write_text("Sword of <Light>")
writer.end_element()
writer.write_element("gold", "250")
writer.end_element()
writer.save("user://inventory.xml")
# <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
# <inventory owner="Ann &amp; Bob">
#   <item id="sword">Sword of &lt;Light&gt;</item>
#   <gold>250</gold>
# </inventory>
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var writer = new XmlWriter();
writer.WriteDeclaration();
writer.BeginElement("inventory");
writer.AddAttribute("owner", "Ann & Bob");
writer.BeginElement("item");
writer.AddAttribute("id", "sword");
writer.WriteText("Sword of <Light>");
writer.EndElement();
writer.WriteElement("gold", "250");
writer.EndElement();
writer.Save("user://inventory.xml");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
The methods return [constant OK] on success, or an error (and print it) if a call does not fit the document, for example [method add_attribute] after a child element, or a second root element.
